    "label": "Mild noise-induced hearing loss (example)",
    "review_status": "engineering",
    "digest": "sha256:951e51a0d942877618f63ff90ff8a681fb8046f50c653b16a91960ca8fa3819d",
    "provenance": "Illustrative permanent mild noise-induced hearing loss, the same in both ears: normal hearing to 1 kHz, a noise notch of 30-35 dB HL from 3 to 6 kHz with the peak at 4 kHz, and partial recovery to 15 dB HL at 8 kHz. It meets the Coles, Lutman and Buffin (2000) notch criteria (3-6 kHz at least 10 dB worse than 1-2 kHz and than 8 kHz), and every threshold is within the BSA mild range (40 dB HL or better). The notch is 10 dB deeper than post_gig_muffled_v1 so the permanent example is audibly stronger than the temporary one. Symmetric ears are an assumption of this example. Calibration matches the other demo presets. Filter workstream example; not audiology-reviewed."
  },
